ity Using Collinearity and Midpoints"} :step/id #uuid "e6dafd2a-98a4-508e-8294-b9f6ffd16d06" :step/math-academy-id 8726}] :activity/title "The Segment Addition Postulate" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186138602}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558658} :activity/id #uuid "63a069e5-dfcc-5dfc-9bdf-efc2c40a433e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050505 :topic/id #uuid "4ed6acfb-fbd7-5e57-abcc-691c74600c49" :topic/math-academy-id 2278} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558582 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62234d9b-3ff8-5dee-be89-1c1d5b6dd819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558054} {:answer/id #uuid "866e0b05-b024-55d0-8a3f-62466373e6a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558128} {:answer/id #uuid "889f2966-4db1-50d6-bdba-0e3b448a1612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558136} {:answer/id #uuid "bf24cb5e-e54e-5a7c-9d8c-7ebfad3e054d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558248} {:answer/id #uuid "c50bf8df-0f2b-5c83-8628-bfa7b5ba4e93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558262}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558128} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7d6781d-d547-56fd-9e7f-2384c91a2d7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "09df5c68-2443-52f1-a65f-9fa7f277dc7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114234" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f22a6d45ad99fa601f45df6d32451c9d004726299130aeb3c6d85e341b275f42.png)\n\nGiven the diagram shown above, what is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "By the segment addition postulate, we have\n\n$$\nAD=AB+BC+CD.\n$$\n\nTo solve for $x,$ we can substitute the given information\n\n$$\nAD=11,\\,AB=2x+3,\\,BC=1-6x,\\,CD=3,\n$$\n\n  \n\nand then solve the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =AB+BC+CD \\\\ 11 & =(2x+3)+(1-6x)+3 \\\\ 11 & =-4x+7 \\\\ 4x & =-4 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "09de0a38-4cd9-52e8-a3ce-8c1afd886d96"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558652 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558499 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0adfc78d-b274-52a3-b385-1cc24a0e4547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557892} {:answer/id #uuid "8303b2c9-e028-58ac-b030-adb4dbf505fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558120} {:answer/id #uuid "dc9623aa-1f66-558c-9dc8-3b3345104e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558302} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e8fb0f-ad49-51be-9c6f-ddad14f234ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558352} {:answer/id #uuid "f89fffb0-f09e-5a27-9b9d-0f4f4f9a72c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558355}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558120} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd21be09-0a94-5fb2-b801-3e3317f3a0d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "26a43956-daac-5057-b186-4e81cc7a6a8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-72048" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb879cc65f75feb37766c28176f4ca8e364dd58410b74e625a75ca3e56b6722f.png)\n\nGiven the diagram shown above, what is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "By the segment addition postulate, we have\n\n$$\nAD=AB+BC+CD.\n$$\n\nTo solve for $x,$ we can substitute the given information\n\n$$\nAD=49,\\,AB=2x+1,\\,BC=3x,\\,CD=8,\n$$\n\n  \n\nand then solve the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =AB+BC+CD \\\\ 49 & =(2x+1)+3x+8 \\\\ 49 & =5x+9 \\\\ 5x & =40 \\\\ x & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8288e638-9825-598a-969c-c812c47b8fa4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558582}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558658 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138832 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9226669b-f95b-5d81-8fa0-34f00060890a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186135941} {:answer/id #uuid "e30cba5b-6769-5bf3-af0c-8e37edf17d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186135942} {:answer/id #uuid "fc081c99-65c2-58e2-a61f-cc6068725780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186135943} {:answer/id #uuid "265433d2-3a5b-564b-9daa-e5f30cacd886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186135944} {:answer/id #uuid "29276cf1-64a6-5a96-bc7a-b06f8006ba08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186135945}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135944} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c78ff5b-52aa-54b9-b865-21f01b6f4d6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186135940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9ea518d5-8976-5fea-b9cf-445893e46637" :question/math-academy-id "q-52749" :question/problem "![](images/d7/d73138fe191ed536299fa6dca679e5948b389d26b4d9e32518eee79123f81f0e.png)\n\nGiven the diagram shown above, what is the measure of $\\overset{―}{BC}?$" :question/worked-solution "The segments addition postulate can be applied to a set of more than three collinear points. In the given situation, it states that\n\n$$\nAD=AB+BC+CD.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known values into the equation above, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =AB+BC+CD \\\\ 28 & =9+BC+7 \\\\ 28 & =16+BC \\\\ 28-16 & =BC \\\\ BC & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9406171b-4e2f-594c-98d9-59cfa7fc7631" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558652}}] :activity/title "The Segment Addition Postulate" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557863}]}
